# One-tree plan, phase 3: a generated 2,000-node graph inside a Cambium tree
# (tree.html?nodes=2000&seed=7).
#
# The same graph and windows p3_presenter_2000 times on index.html with the
# same parameters, shorter than p3_tree_fixture's (see below). The click lands on node 0;
# with 2,000 nodes another may lie over it, so the pick is asserted to be a
# generated node rather than that one.
# Mark ruled the runner's debug build with short windows (2026-09-27): at
# 2,000 nodes it draws a frame every few seconds, so 30-frame windows and 60
# frames to settle, the same on both pages.
log phase 3: 2,000 generated nodes inside a Cambium tree
assert snap nodes == 2000
timing start generated-startup
settle 30
timing stop
wait 30
capture p3_tree_2000_startup
settle 60
timing start generated-steady
settle 30
timing stop
wait 30
click-node https://node-0.generated.test/
settle 2
assert snap picked ~ generated.test
capture p3_tree_2000_picked
